WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.975
Who does what?

2
00:00:00.975 --> 00:00:04.663
Developers build the credential
checks, and need to read Python.

3
00:00:04.663 --> 00:00:10.042
The PKI and credentialing engineers run
the issuing CAs, so they own the list

4
00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:15.337
of CAs by thumbprint, the PIV policy
OIDs, and endpoints that stay available.

5
00:00:15.337 --> 00:00:18.890
And the I S S O keeps
the configuration export,

6
00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:22.538
the findings and every
CRL measurement, dated.

7
00:00:22.538 --> 00:00:25.918
The reader app holds exactly
the three read permissions,

8
00:00:25.918 --> 00:00:28.363
with a certificate or a managed identity.

9
00:00:28.363 --> 00:00:32.740
The code measures and compares; it
never changes the configuration.
